{"question": "Liệu pháp quang động (PDT) có khả năng thúc đẩy sự hình thành ngà sửa chữa trong điều trị tủy buồng (VPT) không?", "claim": "Liệu pháp quang động (PDT) có khả năng kích thích quá trình hình thành ngà sửa chữa và thúc đẩy sự biệt hóa của tế bào gốc tủy răng (DPSC) thành dòng tế bào giống nguyên bào ngà, hỗ trợ hiệu quả cho điều trị tủy buồng.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu ghi nhận PDT thúc đẩy tế bào gốc tủy răng biệt hóa thành dòng nguyên bào ngà và tạo ngà sửa chữa, hiệp đồng tốt với vật liệu che tủy."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "LED-compatible irradiation protocols may improve accessibility. Only after its safety, restorative compatibility, long-term efficacy, and clinical operability have been fully validated can PDT become a standardized clinical strategy across the caries management continuum."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "The ability of PDT to induce reparative dentin formation may be relevant to VPT. In vitro studies have demonstrated that PDT promotes differentiation of DPSCs into an odontoblast-like lineage (Arany et al., 2014; Li et al., 2020; Asnaashari et al., 2022). Moreover, PDT may exert prominent synergistic effects with pulp-capping materials, including mineral trioxide aggregate (MTA), biodentine, and calcium hydroxide (Banci et al., 2020; Zafari et al., 2022). This may be associated with the enhanced formation and deposition of reparative dentin, potentially contributing to more favorable long-term outcomes of pulp capping therapy. Some in vivo studies have reported that, following root canal disinfection with PDT during regenerative endodontic treatment, newly formed tissues may exhibit relatively organized dentinal tubule-like structures (Takahashi et al., 2023). This may be attributed to t"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q3", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "he thorough bacterial elimination and pro-healing effects of PDT on dental pulp tissues, as mentioned above."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Photodynamic therapy for caries management: mechanisms, applications, and perspectives", "heading_path": ["Body", "Conclusions and perspectives"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Photodynamic therapy for caries management: mechanisms, applications, and perspectives", "heading_path": ["Body", "Clinical applications of PDT in caries management", "PDT applications in vital pulp therapy"]}]}
